# Deliberate cost/architecture trade-offs for this single-instance,
# cost-conscious stack (see terraform/roots/stack's own comments for the
# same reasoning applied elsewhere). Re-triage on the next `trivy config`
# drift, not on a schedule.

# SNS topics (operational alerts): payloads are alarm names and one-line
# summaries, not the underlying records; a CMK forces every publisher
# principal into the key policy and turns a misconfigured grant into a
# silently dropped message rather than an error.
AVD-AWS-0095

# S3 buckets (pipeline artifacts, web-build cache): already SSE-S3
# (AES256) encrypted; a CMK adds cost and key-policy upkeep with no
# meaningful gain for build artifacts and an npm tarball cache.
AVD-AWS-0132

# ECR tag mutability is required: the same gramps_web_version tag is
# re-pushed when only the addon set changes (terraform/modules/compute/ecr.tf).
# Running instances pull by digest regardless, so mutability never affects
# what launches.
AVD-AWS-0031

# No WAF in front of CloudFront: single EC2 origin behind CloudFront, no
# NAT gateway, minimal request volume -- WAF's fixed + per-request cost
# outweighs the exposure for this stack's threat model.
AVD-AWS-0011

# Public subnet + open egress: the sole EC2 origin needs outbound access
# (ECR, SSM, package mirrors) and there is no NAT gateway (its ~$32/mo
# fixed cost is the thing being traded away). Ingress is already scoped to
# the CloudFront origin-facing prefix list (modules/network/main.tf).
AVD-AWS-0104
AVD-AWS-0164
